s.... \r\rYou can also prove this directly by computing the star produce of \\Delta\(Y\) with G.)/CreationDate(D:20260327191254+01'00')/F 28/M(D:20260327193215+01'00')/NM(3030b8c8-958c-1348-a5af-7f44a2a0971c)/Name/Comment/Page 5/Popup 67 0 R/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-\weight:normal;font-style:normal">But you can also do this in Matlab. You can compute \(50\) directly for some values of Y.&#13;&#13;You can use lft\(Y*eye\(6\), G\) to compute what the LFR form does.... &#13;&#13;You can also prove this directly by comput\ing the star produce of \\Delta\(Y\) with G.</span></p></body>)/Rect[462.982 547.672 486.982 571.672]/Subj(Sticky Note)/Subtype/Text/T(Roland Toth)/Type/Annot>>endobj67 0 obj<</F 28/Open false/Page 5/Parent 66 0 R/Rect[595.276 479.672 779.276 571.672]/Subtype/Popup/Type/Annot>>endobj68 0 obj<</C[0.988235 0.956863 0.521576]/CA 0.399994/Contents(D_zw is upper triangular. This can be checked when that critical value happens. Can be computed with mussv in Matlab.\r\rmussv\(D_zw, [-6,0]\)\n\nthen you take the  1/upperbound that you computed to see how large Y will make this expression singular.)/CreationDate(D:20260327191709+01'00')/F 4/M(D:20260327192318+01'00')/NM(f5c371ba-3de5-da42-b9ea-c1a0629bb27b)/Page 5/Popup 69 0 R/QuadPoints[242.897 382.09 262.278 382.09 242.897 370.279 262.278 370.279]/RC(<?xml version="1.0"?><body xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:xfa="http://www.xfa.org/schema/xfa-data/1.0/" xfa:APIVersion="Acrobat:25.1.0" xfa:spec="2.0.2" ><p dir="ltr"><span dir="ltr" style="font-size:-14.0pt;text-align:left;color:#000000;font-\weight:normal;font-style:normal">D_zw is upper triangular. This can be checked when that critical value happens. Can be computed with mussv in Matlab.&#13;&#13;mussv\(D_zw, 